[{"name":"MultiGrid","type":"structure","meta":{"uuid":"dba2e831-0ebb-46cf-b9c0-ff3292c6ec58","isGlobalTemplate":false},"configuration":{"columnWidths":[3,9],"layout":{"gap":"L","marginTop":0,"marginBottom":0,"backgroundColor":"transparent"},"visible":true},"content":[{"name":"DetailsList","type":"structure","meta":{"uuid":"9a0ea338-7995-4dfe-adb1-d644a0f6cde5","isGlobalTemplate":false},"configuration":{"visible":true,"layout":{"fullWidth":false,"caretPosition":"right"}},"content":[{"name":"TextCard","type":"content","meta":{"uuid":"610f229a-8d80-4e30-9e59-ef50559c2c6d","isGlobalTemplate":false},"content":{"text":{"htmlDescription":"<div class=\"mb-2\"><p class=\"mb-2\"><strong>For fine shoes with concealed eyelets, such as Oxfords, Derbies and dress shoes, the 2 mm round lace is the right choice: the R2-CS as the classic, or the double-waxed showpiece lace R2-SL from Italy.</strong></p><p class=\"mb-2\"><br></p><p class=\"mb-2\">It steps back visually and leaves the stage to the leather. The lace should pass easily through the eyelet, and the 2 mm round lace is made for the concealed eyelets of classic shoes. The 3 mm round lace (R3-CS) is stronger and belongs on shoes with visible eyelets or hooks, such as lace-up ankle boots.</p><p class=\"mb-2\"><br></p><div class=\"d-flex justify-content-between align-items-center d-md-none bg-light p-2 mb-2 border rounded\"><span class=\"small font-weight-bold text-dark\">&nbsp;<i class=\"fa fa-hand-o-right text-muted mr-1\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> Round laces compared&nbsp;</span> <span class=\"badge badge-secondary py-1 px-2\">&nbsp;<i class=\"fa fa-arrows-h mr-1\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> Swipe sideways&nbsp;</span></div></div><div class=\"laccico-scroll-wrapper\"><div class=\"table-responsive laccico-scroll-table\"><table class=\"table table-bordered table-hover text-left mb-0\" style=\"border: 1px solid #000000; font-size: 0.9rem; min-width: 560px;\"><thead class=\"thead-dark\" style=\"background-color: #000000; color: #ffffff;\"><tr><th scope=\"col\" class=\"py-3 px-3\">Lace</th><th scope=\"col\" class=\"py-3 px-3\">Effect</th><th scope=\"col\" class=\"py-3 px-3\">Shoes</th><th scope=\"col\" class=\"py-3 px-3\">Lengths</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class=\"py-3 px-3 align-middle text-nowrap\"><a href=\"/en/shape-diameter/round-laces-by-diameter/round-laces-2-mm/r2-cs\" class=\"font-weight-bold text-dark d-block\" style=\"text-decoration: underline;\">R2-CS</a></td><td class=\"py-3 px-3 align-middle\">Silky-matt sheen, steps back.</td><td class=\"py-3 px-3 align-middle\">Oxfords, Derbies, business shoes for every day.</td><td class=\"py-3 px-3 align-middle\">45–180 cm</td></tr><tr><td class=\"py-3 px-3 align-middle text-nowrap\"><a href=\"/en/shape-diameter/round-laces-by-diameter/round-laces-2-mm/r2-sl\" class=\"font-weight-bold text-dark d-block\" style=\"text-decoration: underline;\">R2-SL</a></td><td class=\"py-3 px-3 align-middle\">Double-waxed, special depth of colour, splendid sheen.</td><td class=\"py-3 px-3 align-middle\">Fine Goodyear-welted shoes in box calf or shell cordovan, evening shoes.</td><td class=\"py-3 px-3 align-middle\">45–180 cm</td></tr><tr><td class=\"py-3 px-3 align-middle text-nowrap\"><a href=\"/en/shape-diameter/round-laces-by-diameter/round-laces-3-mm\" class=\"font-weight-bold text-dark d-block\" style=\"text-decoration: underline;\">R3-CS</a></td><td class=\"py-3 px-3 align-middle\">Stronger, the round cord is clearly visible.</td><td class=\"py-3 px-3 align-middle\">Lace-up ankle boots and low shoes with visible eyelets or hooks.</td><td class=\"py-3 px-3 align-middle\">45–150 cm</td></tr></tbody></table></div></div>","textAlignment":"left","color":""},"button":{"label":"","link":"","variant":"primary"},"layout":{"backgroundColor":"","paddingTop":0,"paddingBottom":0,"paddingLeft":0,"paddingRight":0}},"configuration":{"visible":true,"detailsSettings":{"label":"Which round laces are suitable for fine men's shoes?","defaultOpen":false}}},{"name":"TextCard","type":"content","meta":{"uuid":"8a94ebe6-b5d4-4a02-b9c1-6343e130b2b3","isGlobalTemplate":false},"content":{"text":{"htmlDescription":"<div class=\"mb-2\"><p class=\"mb-2\"><strong>For business shoes with concealed eyelets, choose the 3 mm flat lace (F3-CS). It is our finest flat lace and sets a quiet accent where the 2 mm round lace steps back completely.</strong></p><p class=\"mb-2\"><br></p><p class=\"mb-2\">If Derbies or full brogues have visible eyelets with a metal ring on the outside, the 4 mm flat lace (F4-CS) is the right choice. It is particularly popular on lace-up ankle boots with eyelets and hooks. Both come in 60, 75, 90 and 120 cm.</p><p class=\"mb-2\"><br></p><div class=\"d-flex justify-content-between align-items-center d-md-none bg-light p-2 mb-2 border rounded\"><span class=\"small font-weight-bold text-dark\">&nbsp;<i class=\"fa fa-hand-o-right text-muted mr-1\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> Flat laces compared&nbsp;</span> <span class=\"badge badge-secondary py-1 px-2\">&nbsp;<i class=\"fa fa-arrows-h mr-1\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> Swipe sideways&nbsp;</span></div></div><div class=\"laccico-scroll-wrapper\"><div class=\"table-responsive laccico-scroll-table\"><table class=\"table table-bordered table-hover text-left mb-0\" style=\"border: 1px solid #000000; font-size: 0.9rem; min-width: 560px;\"><thead class=\"thead-dark\" style=\"background-color: #000000; color: #ffffff;\"><tr><th scope=\"col\" class=\"py-3 px-3\">Lace</th><th scope=\"col\" class=\"py-3 px-3\">Eyelets</th><th scope=\"col\" class=\"py-3 px-3\">Shoes</th><th scope=\"col\" class=\"py-3 px-3\">Lengths</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class=\"py-3 px-3 align-middle text-nowrap\"><a href=\"/en/shape-diameter/flat-laces-by-width/flat-laces-3-mm\" class=\"font-weight-bold text-dark d-block\" style=\"text-decoration: underline;\">F3-CS</a></td><td class=\"py-3 px-3 align-middle\">Concealed eyelets.</td><td class=\"py-3 px-3 align-middle\">Oxfords, slim Derbies, dress shoes.</td><td class=\"py-3 px-3 align-middle\">60–120 cm</td></tr><tr><td class=\"py-3 px-3 align-middle text-nowrap\"><a href=\"/en/shape-diameter/flat-laces-by-width/flat-laces-4-mm\" class=\"font-weight-bold text-dark d-block\" style=\"text-decoration: underline;\">F4-CS</a></td><td class=\"py-3 px-3 align-middle\">Visible eyelets.</td><td class=\"py-3 px-3 align-middle\">Derbies and full brogues with visible eyelets, lace-up ankle boots with hooks.</td><td class=\"py-3 px-3 align-middle\">60–120 cm</td></tr></tbody></table></div></div>","textAlignment":"left","color":""},"button":{"label":"","link":"","variant":"primary"},"layout":{"backgroundColor":"","paddingTop":0,"paddingBottom":0,"paddingLeft":0,"paddingRight":0}},"configuration":{"visible":true,"detailsSettings":{"label":"Which shoelace width do you choose for modern business shoes?","defaultOpen":false}}},{"name":"TextCard","type":"content","meta":{"uuid":"47ad38c4-c554-488e-b5a5-ed1e263aebaf","isGlobalTemplate":false},"content":{"text":{"htmlDescription":"<div class=\"mb-2\"><p class=\"mb-2\"><strong>Classic Goodyear-welted low shoes with concealed eyelets call for fine laces: the 2 mm round lace or the 3 mm flat lace. Not every welted shoe needs a fine lace, though.</strong></p><p class=\"mb-2\"><br></p><p class=\"mb-2\">Country Derbies, lace-up ankle boots and boots with visible eyelets or hooks are also Goodyear-welted. They take stronger laces, such as the 3 mm round lace or the 4 mm flat lace. On Oxfords with concealed eyelets, straight lacing is the classic: you only see horizontal bars.</p><p class=\"mb-2\"><br></p><div class=\"d-flex justify-content-between align-items-center d-md-none bg-light p-2 mb-2 border rounded\"><span class=\"small font-weight-bold text-dark\">&nbsp;<i class=\"fa fa-hand-o-right text-muted mr-1\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> Shape by shoe&nbsp;</span> <span class=\"badge badge-secondary py-1 px-2\">&nbsp;<i class=\"fa fa-arrows-h mr-1\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> Swipe sideways&nbsp;</span></div></div><div class=\"laccico-scroll-wrapper\"><div class=\"table-responsive laccico-scroll-table\"><table class=\"table table-bordered table-hover text-left mb-0\" style=\"border: 1px solid #000000; font-size: 0.9rem; min-width: 560px;\"><thead class=\"thead-dark\" style=\"background-color: #000000; color: #ffffff;\"><tr><th scope=\"col\" class=\"py-3 px-3\">Shoe</th><th scope=\"col\" class=\"py-3 px-3\">Eyelets</th><th scope=\"col\" class=\"py-3 px-3\">Lace</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class=\"font-weight-bold py-3 px-3 align-middle text-nowrap\">Oxford<br><span class=\"small text-muted font-weight-normal\">Closed lacing</span></td><td class=\"py-3 px-3 align-middle\">Concealed eyelets.</td><td class=\"py-3 px-3 align-middle text-nowrap\"><a href=\"/en/shape-diameter/round-laces-by-diameter/round-laces-2-mm/r2-cs\" class=\"font-weight-bold text-dark\" style=\"text-decoration: underline;\">R2-CS</a> · <a href=\"/en/shape-diameter/round-laces-by-diameter/round-laces-2-mm/r2-sl\" class=\"font-weight-bold text-dark\" style=\"text-decoration: underline;\">R2-SL</a> · <a href=\"/en/shape-diameter/flat-laces-by-width/flat-laces-3-mm\" class=\"font-weight-bold text-dark\" style=\"text-decoration: underline;\">F3-CS</a></td></tr><tr><td class=\"font-weight-bold py-3 px-3 align-middle text-nowrap\">Derby<br><span class=\"small text-muted font-weight-normal\">Open lacing</span></td><td class=\"py-3 px-3 align-middle\">Concealed eyelets.</td><td class=\"py-3 px-3 align-middle text-nowrap\"><a href=\"/en/shape-diameter/round-laces-by-diameter/round-laces-2-mm/r2-cs\" class=\"font-weight-bold text-dark\" style=\"text-decoration: underline;\">R2-CS</a> · <a href=\"/en/shape-diameter/round-laces-by-diameter/round-laces-2-mm/r2-sl\" class=\"font-weight-bold text-dark\" style=\"text-decoration: underline;\">R2-SL</a> · <a href=\"/en/shape-diameter/flat-laces-by-width/flat-laces-3-mm\" class=\"font-weight-bold text-dark\" style=\"text-decoration: underline;\">F3-CS</a></td></tr><tr><td class=\"font-weight-bold py-3 px-3 align-middle text-nowrap\">Full brogue<br><span class=\"small text-muted font-weight-normal\">Perforations</span></td><td class=\"py-3 px-3 align-middle\">Concealed eyelets.</td><td class=\"py-3 px-3 align-middle text-nowrap\"><a href=\"/en/shape-diameter/round-laces-by-diameter/round-laces-2-mm/r2-cs\" class=\"font-weight-bold text-dark\" style=\"text-decoration: underline;\">R2-CS</a> · <a href=\"/en/shape-diameter/round-laces-by-diameter/round-laces-2-mm/r2-sl\" class=\"font-weight-bold text-dark\" style=\"text-decoration: underline;\">R2-SL</a> · <a href=\"/en/shape-diameter/flat-laces-by-width/flat-laces-3-mm\" class=\"font-weight-bold text-dark\" style=\"text-decoration: underline;\">F3-CS</a></td></tr><tr><td class=\"font-weight-bold py-3 px-3 align-middle text-nowrap\">Country Derby<br><span class=\"small text-muted font-weight-normal\">Sturdy leather</span></td><td class=\"py-3 px-3 align-middle\">Visible eyelets.</td><td class=\"py-3 px-3 align-middle text-nowrap\"><a href=\"/en/shape-diameter/round-laces-by-diameter/round-laces-3-mm\" class=\"font-weight-bold text-dark\" style=\"text-decoration: underline;\">R3-CS</a> · <a href=\"/en/shape-diameter/flat-laces-by-width/flat-laces-4-mm\" class=\"font-weight-bold text-dark\" style=\"text-decoration: underline;\">F4-CS</a></td></tr><tr><td class=\"font-weight-bold py-3 px-3 align-middle text-nowrap\">Lace-up ankle boot<br><span class=\"small text-muted font-weight-normal\">Ankle-high</span></td><td class=\"py-3 px-3 align-middle\">Eyelets below, hooks above.</td><td class=\"py-3 px-3 align-middle text-nowrap\"><a href=\"/en/shape-diameter/round-laces-by-diameter/round-laces-3-mm\" class=\"font-weight-bold text-dark\" style=\"text-decoration: underline;\">R3-CS</a> · <a href=\"/en/shape-diameter/flat-laces-by-width/flat-laces-4-mm\" class=\"font-weight-bold text-dark\" style=\"text-decoration: underline;\">F4-CS</a></td></tr></tbody></table></div></div>","textAlignment":"left","color":""},"button":{"label":"","link":"","variant":"primary"},"layout":{"backgroundColor":"","paddingTop":0,"paddingBottom":0,"paddingLeft":0,"paddingRight":0}},"configuration":{"visible":true,"detailsSettings":{"label":"Which type of shoelace belongs in Goodyear-welted leather shoes?","defaultOpen":false}}},{"name":"TextCard","type":"content","meta":{"uuid":"215876b1-4e36-471e-89de-b6ee7bec93f4","isGlobalTemplate":false},"content":{"text":{"htmlDescription":"<div class=\"mb-2\"><p class=\"mb-2\"><strong>Classic business shoes with 4 to 5 pairs of eyelets take 75 cm, with 5 to 6 pairs of eyelets 90 cm. The safest way is to measure your old laces unlaced, from tip to tip.</strong></p><p class=\"mb-2\"><br></p><p class=\"mb-2\">For the classic 5-eyelet Derby or Oxford, 75 cm is the norm; for a wider foot, 90 cm is the better choice. Derbies with low-set lacing panels and short lacing need 60 cm. For women's sizes, one size shorter is often enough.</p><p class=\"mb-2\"><br></p><div class=\"d-flex justify-content-between align-items-center d-md-none bg-light p-2 mb-2 border rounded\"><span class=\"small font-weight-bold text-dark\">&nbsp;<i class=\"fa fa-hand-o-right text-muted mr-1\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> Lengths&nbsp;</span> <span class=\"badge badge-secondary py-1 px-2\">&nbsp;<i class=\"fa fa-arrows-h mr-1\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> Swipe sideways&nbsp;</span></div></div><div class=\"laccico-scroll-wrapper\"><div class=\"table-responsive laccico-scroll-table\"><table class=\"table table-bordered table-hover text-left mb-0\" style=\"border: 1px solid #000000; font-size: 0.9rem; min-width: 560px;\"><thead class=\"thead-dark\" style=\"background-color: #000000; color: #ffffff;\"><tr><th scope=\"col\" class=\"py-3 px-3\">Lacing</th><th scope=\"col\" class=\"py-3 px-3\">Length</th><th scope=\"col\" class=\"py-3 px-3\">Typical shoes</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class=\"font-weight-bold py-3 px-3 align-middle text-nowrap\">Short lacing<br><span class=\"small text-muted font-weight-normal\">Low-set</span></td><td class=\"py-3 px-3 align-middle\">60 cm</td><td class=\"py-3 px-3 align-middle\">Derbies with few pairs of holes.</td></tr><tr><td class=\"font-weight-bold py-3 px-3 align-middle text-nowrap\">4–5 pairs of eyelets<br><span class=\"small text-muted font-weight-normal\">Normal case</span></td><td class=\"py-3 px-3 align-middle\">75 cm</td><td class=\"py-3 px-3 align-middle\">The classic 5-eyelet Derby or Oxford.</td></tr><tr><td class=\"font-weight-bold py-3 px-3 align-middle text-nowrap\">5–6 pairs of eyelets<br><span class=\"small text-muted font-weight-normal\">Wider foot</span></td><td class=\"py-3 px-3 align-middle\">90 cm</td><td class=\"py-3 px-3 align-middle\">Same shoe, more volume at the instep.</td></tr><tr><td class=\"font-weight-bold py-3 px-3 align-middle text-nowrap\">Lace-up ankle boot<br><span class=\"small text-muted font-weight-normal\">Ankle-high</span></td><td class=\"py-3 px-3 align-middle\">120 cm</td><td class=\"py-3 px-3 align-middle\">Fine ankle boots with many pairs of eyelets.</td></tr></tbody></table></div></div><p>More on our <a href=\"/en/laccico-finest-waxed-laces/shoelace-length\" style=\"color:#1A1A1A;font-weight:600;text-decoration:underline\">Shoelace length</a> page.</p>","textAlignment":"left","color":""},"button":{"label":"","link":"","variant":"primary"},"layout":{"backgroundColor":"","paddingTop":0,"paddingBottom":0,"paddingLeft":0,"paddingRight":0}},"configuration":{"visible":true,"detailsSettings":{"label":"What shoelace length do business shoes need?","defaultOpen":false}}},{"name":"TextCard","type":"content","meta":{"uuid":"baa694c2-8734-455a-b648-1773ff533050","isGlobalTemplate":false},"content":{"text":{"htmlDescription":"<div class=\"mb-2\"><p class=\"mb-2\"><strong>For formal occasions such as weddings, galas or evening wear, the double-waxed 2 mm round lace Splendore di Laccico (R2-SL) is the right choice. It has a special depth of colour and a splendid sheen like fine calfskin.</strong></p><p class=\"mb-2\"><br></p><p class=\"mb-2\">On Goodyear-welted Oxfords in box calf or shell cordovan it simply belongs, like cufflinks with a dinner jacket. With a dark suit at the office, the R2-CS with its silky-matt sheen also fits. Choose the colour tone-on-tone with the leather.</p><p class=\"mb-2\"><br></p><div class=\"d-flex justify-content-between align-items-center d-md-none bg-light p-2 mb-2 border rounded\"><span class=\"small font-weight-bold text-dark\">&nbsp;<i class=\"fa fa-hand-o-right text-muted mr-1\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> Occasion&nbsp;</span> <span class=\"badge badge-secondary py-1 px-2\">&nbsp;<i class=\"fa fa-arrows-h mr-1\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> Swipe sideways&nbsp;</span></div></div><div class=\"laccico-scroll-wrapper\"><div class=\"table-responsive laccico-scroll-table\"><table class=\"table table-bordered table-hover text-left mb-0\" style=\"border: 1px solid #000000; font-size: 0.9rem; min-width: 560px;\"><thead class=\"thead-dark\" style=\"background-color: #000000; color: #ffffff;\"><tr><th scope=\"col\" class=\"py-3 px-3\">Occasion</th><th scope=\"col\" class=\"py-3 px-3\">Lace</th><th scope=\"col\" class=\"py-3 px-3\">Colour</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class=\"font-weight-bold py-3 px-3 align-middle text-nowrap\">Wedding &amp; gala<br><span class=\"small text-muted font-weight-normal\">Black tie</span></td><td class=\"py-3 px-3 align-middle text-nowrap\"><a href=\"/en/shape-diameter/round-laces-by-diameter/round-laces-2-mm/r2-sl\" class=\"font-weight-bold text-dark d-block\" style=\"text-decoration: underline;\">R2-SL</a></td><td class=\"py-3 px-3 align-middle\">Nero (black) with black evening shoes.</td></tr><tr><td class=\"font-weight-bold py-3 px-3 align-middle text-nowrap\">Formal suit<br><span class=\"small text-muted font-weight-normal\">Daytime</span></td><td class=\"py-3 px-3 align-middle text-nowrap\"><a href=\"/en/shape-diameter/round-laces-by-diameter/round-laces-2-mm/r2-sl\" class=\"font-weight-bold text-dark d-block\" style=\"text-decoration: underline;\">R2-SL</a></td><td class=\"py-3 px-3 align-middle\">Tone-on-tone with the leather, black or brown.</td></tr><tr><td class=\"font-weight-bold py-3 px-3 align-middle text-nowrap\">Dark suit<br><span class=\"small text-muted font-weight-normal\">Office</span></td><td class=\"py-3 px-3 align-middle text-nowrap\"><a href=\"/en/shape-diameter/round-laces-by-diameter/round-laces-2-mm/r2-cs\" class=\"font-weight-bold text-dark d-block\" style=\"text-decoration: underline;\">R2-CS</a></td><td class=\"py-3 px-3 align-middle\">Black, dark brown or navy.</td></tr></tbody></table></div></div>","textAlignment":"left","color":""},"button":{"label":"","link":"","variant":"primary"},"layout":{"backgroundColor":"","paddingTop":0,"paddingBottom":0,"paddingLeft":0,"paddingRight":0}},"configuration":{"visible":true,"detailsSettings":{"label":"Which shoelaces are suitable for formal shoes for weddings and galas?","defaultOpen":false}}}],"parent_slot":0},{"name":"MultiGrid","type":"structure","meta":{"uuid":"435c3198-ac14-4b72-93a1-13e4d9496ca5","isGlobalTemplate":false},"configuration":{"columnWidths":[6,6],"layout":{"gap":"L","marginTop":0,"marginBottom":0,"backgroundColor":"transparent"},"visible":true},"content":[{"name":"CategoryData","type":"content","meta":{"uuid":"0063fc1c-1e87-43e8-b9e4-2cf3df0e4883","isGlobalTemplate":false},"content":{"name":"","fields":{"name":true,"description1":true,"description2":false,"shortDescription":false},"fieldsOrder":["name","description1","description2","shortDescription"],"fieldsDisabled":[],"displayCategoryImage":"off","image":{"fillMode":"fill","alt":"","brightness":0.75},"text":{"color":"#121212","bgColor":"#fbfbf9","bgOpacity":1,"textAlignment":"left","justify":"top","align":"left","background":false},"layout":{"paddingTop":16,"paddingBottom":16,"paddingLeft":0,"paddingRight":0}},"parent_slot":0},{"name":"Image","type":"content","meta":{"uuid":"8499b9cc-8152-4